 ## Installation
 
+### Linux measurement logs
+
+Guest report construction reads the firmware TCG2 log and the systemd
+JSON-sequence log at `/run/log/systemd/tpm2-measure.log`. Genuine phase records
+for selected PCR 11 are appended as EV_IPL entries, with every recorded bank
+digest checked against the measured string. Phase order is retained; there is
+no fixed boot-phase transcript. Unsupported selected userspace event types or
+banks and malformed/unreadable logs fail explicitly.
+
+SHA-256 static PCR replay and the quote's selected-PCR digest must match the
+collected PCR values. One-shot attestation recollects at most three times when
+measurements change or the log has not caught up; decomposed report construction
+returns the consistency error to its caller. A missing userspace log is allowed
+only if firmware-only replay still matches. Dynamic PCR reset states are not
+replayed by this check. These checks do not independently authenticate the AK
+signature or establish challenge-bound quote freshness.
+
+The low-level `guest_attest::collect_tcg_logs` helper now takes the selected PCR
+indices and returns `io::Result<Vec<u8>>`; callers must handle collection errors.
+Windows collection behavior is unchanged.
+
 Add to your `Cargo.toml`:
 
 ```toml
